From: Amphoze <184834775+Amphoze@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 11:27:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] stores: snippets private per member, shared per project

The snippet store is kept under the request's project directory on the data volume:
<ref>/snippets/<P>/ for a member's own (P: the SHA-256 of the principal's length-prefixed
issuer and subject), <ref>/snippets/shared/<P>/ for what that member shared. Nothing of the
request names a directory. Shared snippets are readable by every member and changed by their
author only; a read_only member reads and saves nothing. A shared snippet's id is derived by
SHA-256 from its author and name and never equals a member's own. Links and non-regular
files are never followed or read; files are written by rename. Per project, at most
snippet_entries entries and snippet_bytes bytes, checked and written under the project's
lock. A snippet, and the SQL of one listing, are at most result_bytes; a listing past it ends
with a cursor of the sort key and id of its last snippet. An answer that carries SQL is made
and sent in one of four slots of the process, two at most for a project, held until its body
has been taken or cut (the client gone, an error, handover_ms); a request waits a bounded
time behind a bounded queue, else 429 busy. A write whose id another of
the member's snippets has, and a rename, move or share onto a taken name, are 409 exists.
The process-wide snippets folder and its setting are gone.
